@using Plantry.Web.Pages.Today
@model IndexModel

@* Today stats widget (plantry-h9z9, stats-page-prototype.html appendix "Today" injection point):
   one rotating "did you know" fact plus the household's streak chips. Only rendered by Index.cshtml
   when !IsColdStart, and TodayStats is always populated in that case (TodayStatsService never returns
   null — see TodayStatsVm's doc comment) — so no empty/onboard state is needed here, unlike
   _ExpiringWidget's three-state shape. Deliberately a single small card, never a dashboard takeover:
   one fact line + a chip row, both reusing existing primitives (.today-cta__sub, .chip-row/.chip-stat)
   with no new CSS beyond the shared .chip-row wrapper.

   No footer link to /Stats: that route belongs to plantry-zjsu (Stats dashboard page), which is not
   built yet — see the comment thread on plantry-h9z9/plantry-zjsu. Re-add a "See your stats" footer
   link here once /Stats exists. *@
<div class="today-widget" id="today-stats-widget">
    <div class="today-widget__head">
        <h3>Did you know?</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="today-widget__body">
        <p class="today-cta__sub">@Model.TodayStats!.RotatingFactText</p>
        @if (Model.TodayStats.StreakChips.Count > 0)
        {
            <div class="chip-row">
                @foreach (var chip in Model.TodayStats.StreakChips)
                {
                    <span class="chip-stat">@chip.Icon <b>@chip.Value</b> @chip.Label</span>
                }
            </div>
        }
    </div>
</div>
